rumik-oss-1-int4 (this repository): further modifications, 2026-11-06
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived from rumik-ai/rumik-oss-1 (above) by post-training quantization only;
no training or fine-tuning, and the vocabulary and architecture are unchanged.

  1. All attention and MLP projection weights of the 36 decoder layers
     (q, k, v, o, gate, up, down) quantized to 4-bit integers: groups of
     128 input columns, min/max round-to-nearest, w = code * scale + min,
     two codes per byte (low nibble = even column), fp16 scale and min
     per group. Mean relative weight error 10.5% (see export.json).
  2. Input embedding table quantized to int8 with one fp16 scale per row
     (relative error 1.0%).
  3. Output head: only the 16,385 audio rows (Mimi codes + </audio>) are
     kept, in bf16, with their token ids (head.audio_ids); the text rows are
     dropped, because the model only emits audio tokens after <audio>.
  4. Layer norms and the stop predictor are unchanged (copied as-is).
  5. The Mimi codec, tokenizer and config are not included here; use the
     original repository (rumik-ai/rumik-oss-1).
